Based on your input, here's a complete N8N workflow design with detailed node configurations:

## Workflow Overview
**Name:** Webhook to Email and Database Update
**Description:** Receives webhook data, sends an email notification, and updates a database record

## Node Configurations

### 1. Webhook Trigger Node
```json
{
  "name": "Webhook Trigger",
  "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
  "parameters": {
    "httpMethod": "POST",
    "path": "webhook-endpoint",
    "responseMode": "responseNode",
    "options": {
      "rawBody": false,
      "allowedOrigins": "*"
    }
  },
  "position": [240, 300],
  "webhookId": "auto-generated"
}
```

### 2. Send Email Node
```json
{
  "name": "Send Email",
  "type": "n8n-nodes-base.emailSend",
  "parameters": {
    "fromEmail": "noreply@yourcompany.com",
    "toEmail": "={{ $json.email || 'admin@yourcompany.com' }}",
    "subject": "Webhook Notification: {{ $json.subject || 'New Data Received' }}",
    "message": "Hello,\n\nA new webhook has been received with the following data:\n\n{{ JSON.stringify($json, null, 2) }}\n\nBest regards,\nAutomation System",
    "options": {
      "ccEmail": "",
      "bccEmail": "",
      "replyTo": "",
      "priority": "normal",
      "attachments": "=[]"
    }
  },
  "position": [480, 200],
  "credentials": {
    "smtp": {
      "id": "smtp-credentials",
      "name": "SMTP Account"
    }
  }
}
```

### 3. Update Database Node
```json
{
  "name": "Update Database",
  "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
  "parameters": {
    "operation": "executeQuery",
    "query": "INSERT INTO webhook_data (data, email, timestamp, status) VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET data = $1, email = $2, timestamp = $3, status = $4",
    "additionalFields": {
      "mode": "independently",
      "queryParameters": "={{ [\n  JSON.stringify($json),\n  $json.email || null,\n  new Date().toISOString(),\n  'processed'\n] }}"
    }
  },
  "position": [480, 400],
  "credentials": {
    "postgres": {
      "id": "postgres-credentials",
      "name": "PostgreSQL Database"
    }
  }
}
```

### 4. Response Node
```json
{
  "name": "Webhook Response",
  "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
  "parameters": {
    "respondWith": "json",
    "responseBody": "={{ {\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"message\": \"Webhook processed successfully\",\n  \"timestamp\": new Date().toISOString(),\n  \"processed_data\": {\n    \"email_sent\": true,\n    \"database_updated\": true\n  }\n} }}",
    "options": {
      "responseCode": 200,
      "responseHeaders": {
        "Content-Type": "application/json"
      }
    }
  },
  "position": [720, 300]
}
```

## Workflow Connections
```json
{
  "connections": {
    "Webhook Trigger": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Send Email",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          },
          {
            "node": "Update Database",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Send Email": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Webhook Response",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Update Database": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Webhook Response",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

## Error Handling Enhancement (Optional)

### Add Error Handling Node
```json
{
  "name": "Error Handler",
  "type": "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
  "parameters": {},
  "position": [480, 500]
}
```

### Error Response Node
```json
{
  "name": "Error Response",
  "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
  "parameters": {
    "respondWith": "json",
    "responseBody": "={{ {\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"error\": $json.error.message,\n  \"timestamp\": new Date().toISOString()\n} }}",
    "options": {
      "responseCode": 500
    }
  },
  "position": [720, 500]
}
```

## Setup Requirements

### Credentials Needed:
1. **SMTP Credentials** for email sending
2. **Database Credentials** (PostgreSQL shown, but can be MySQL, MongoDB, etc.)

### Environment Variables:
```bash
N8N_BASIC_AUTH_ACTIVE=true
N8N_BASIC_AUTH_USER=admin
N8N_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD=your_password
WEBHOOK_URL=https://your-n8n-instance.com/webhook/webhook-endpoint
```

### Database Schema (if using PostgreSQL):
```sql
CREATE TABLE webhook_data (
  id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
  data JSONB,
  email VARCHAR(255),
  timestamp TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),
  status VARCHAR(50)
);
```

## Testing the Workflow

### Sample Webhook Payload:
```bash
curl -X POST https://your-n8n-instance.com/webhook/webhook-endpoint \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "subject": "Test Notification",
    "user_id": 12345,
    "action": "user_registration",
    "data": {
      "name": "John Doe",
      "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z"
    }
  }'
```

This workflow will:
1. Receive the webhook data
2. Send an email notification with the webhook payload
3. Insert/update the data in the database
4. Return a success response to the webhook caller
5. Handle errors gracefully if any step fails

